{title: Blessed Assurance}
{key: C}
{x_theme: blood, salvation, grace-mercy}
{x_source: chrd:blessed_assurance.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
This is my [C]story, [F]this is my [C]song,
Praising my [Am7]Sa  -  [G]vior [D]all the day [G]long;
[G7]This is my [C]story, [F]this is my [C]song,
Praising my [Dm]Savior [G]all the day [C]long.

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]Blessed assurance, [F]Jesus is [C]mine!
O what a [Am7]fore - [G]taste of [D]glory di[G]vine!
Heir of sal[C]vation, [F]purchase of [C]God,
Born of his [Dm]Spirit, [G]washed in his [C]blood.

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]Perfect submission, [F]perfect [C]delight,
Visions of [Am7]rap  -  [G]ture  [D]now burst on my [G]sight;
Angels des[C]cending  [F]bring from a[C]bove,
Echoes of [Dm]mercy, [G]whispers of [C]love.

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]Perfect submission, [F]all is [C]at rest;
I in my [Am7]Sa  -  [G]vior [D]am happy and [G]blessed,
Watching and [C]waiting, [F]looking a[C]bove,
[C]Filled with his [Dm]goodness, [G]lost in his [C]love.
